Yes. This class is just a different kind of wizard. personally I think
that the difference between classes is not what item they use but the
fact that they make you play the game a little differently. A barbarian
and a rogue could use the same weapons, but a rogue will be a ranged
fighter and a barbarian melee, because of the small differences between
them.

My idea for a bard class was to allow them to charm monsters with their
music. Different instruments charm different creatures (flutes ->
snakes for example). You'd still need fighting skills for the creatures
you can't charm. Music charm could be temporary also.

You could even allow different effects depending on tune (scare,
pacify, charm, conflict, sleep, etc). Effects would have to be heard to
work, so deaf creatures are inmune (and allowing temporary deafness,
like from the bang of a grenade). This would preclude effects like
remove curse and such. You could even do maintained effects. Play a
charm tune for N turns to make the snakes help you against the ants.

These would of course rely on a music skill, maybe instrument based. So
you can have a flute bard, a bugle bard, a grand-piano bard, etc. Or a
harp-playing ranger, drum-playing barbarian, etc.

Additionally Bards would be able to get special effects from magical
instruments. Fireballs from fire horns, for example.

And you'd need to find someone to teach you the tunes (to avoid trying
them out in the heat of battle). Probably allies in the quest level, or
gypsies in [s].

So basically a bard would be a healer-level fighter, barbarian-level
spellcaster that can have more pets and even get some of the enemies to
help him sometimes. Figurines and turn undead become a very useful
source of allies. But, do you heal your temporary-allies or let them
get hurt so you can finish them off when the charm wears off?

BTW, there's a bard patch out there, but I can't find spoilers for it.

Quest artifact would be something to play against higher-level
creatures. For pacifying demons, for example. Or maybe it works on all
creatures but is harder to use. #invoke could tell you tunes for your
instruments.



